WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.980
We can use unison, too, you know!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.980
The lunar surface tag 
battle's about to begin!

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.970
Something we can't even imagine 
must be happening on the moon.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.170
Simultaneous attacks...

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.780
But we can do that, too!

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.330
We've passed Omaezaki.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.990
We're about to reach the operation point.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.920
Tsubasa-san, Maria-san, we're going 
to hit Yggdrasil with everything we've got.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.000
So...

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.220
<i>We'll come back! We promise!</i>

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.820
<i>Until then, keep Earth safe!</i>

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.610
Yggdrasil is active!

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.000
It's encroaching on the 
Earth's core from all directions.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.060
Everyone's been able to 
protect the Curse of Balal.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.810
So why is Yggdrasil...

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.560
It's probably her.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.610
Commander, where are you going?

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.860
With the Wielders away,

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.190
the only thing that can stand against 
that myth-class monster is...

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:04.450
Wait.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.790
What do you mean "stand against"?

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.260
I have an idea!

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.310
The great Metempsychosis 
will soon take place.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.350
After I convert the lost children 
of this planet into my own power,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.780
I shall strike at my fellows
 who fled beyond the horizon.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.440
<b>Episode 12
Senki Zessho</b>

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.190
I can't control the beating of my heart.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.470
Yes, indeed.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:43.320
At times like these, humans hum a song.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.030
A single girl standing 
in the distant wastes...

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.260
<i>Are you scared?</i>

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.250
I'm so scared I can barely stand.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.140
But...

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.830
Miku-san didn't run.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:07.170
So I don't want to run, even if I'm scared.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.090
And right now, I'm not alone!

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.310
Reckless.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.530
So there are still fools 
who would challenge me.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.620
I agree.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.370
Regardless, don't underestimate my alchemy.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.070
<i>Crushing this infuriating, unchanging world</i>

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:05.310
<i>Do you need a monster? Answer me!</i>

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:05.520
Pathetic. Where are you even aiming?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.860
<i>These troublesome feelings without an answer</i>

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.880
Not a bad idea.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.330
So you're aiming for 
Yggdrasil's trunk, not me.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:15.330
<i>Where is my prey to devour?</i>

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:21.200
<i>I don't care about gods or evil</i>

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.750
Carol's alchemy was a challenge to the gods.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.560
But since that power burns away memories...

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.560
<i>The place I stand is everything</i>

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:35.620
<i>I'll forgive love, hate
 and your incomplete race</i>

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:40.910
<i>A sforzando that burns the 
remnants of memories to ash</i>

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.580
Did you think I couldn't dodge them
 if you fired that many?

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:42.800
A human's power isn't
 enough to shoot me down!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.950
<i>A symphony that surpasses numerical formulas,</i>

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.910
<i>the rules of composition for destruction</i>

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:49.740
<i>That day that told me to—</i>

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.240
Meaningless.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.360
But more than that...

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.000
Infuriating!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:10.350
<i>My songs don't come cheap</i>

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.130
I can't move...

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.320
You bound me?

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:26.570
Your use of impossible 
physics nullifies damage.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.120
But what about bondage?

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.450
Alcahest!

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.750
I have an idea.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.410
Our ultimate weapon is 
an alchemy that recreates

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:47.580
a limited version of the world dissection 
capability of the Château de Tiffauges.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.170
Carol said that, yes.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.750
If that could fight against a god, then...

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:58.980
Do you intend to use that to 
atone for killing your friends?

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.980
I've long since finished analyzing 
the concept of humanity.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:09.510
So I merely categorize any other impurities 
as "gods," then dissect them.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.860
Don't underestimate my alchemy!

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.010
But to make it as easy as you say,

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.540
you'll need incredible energy.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.090
Where will you get it?

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:21.610
The incineration of memories!

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:26.260
If you don't have enough, 
burn my memories, too!

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:40.770
Did she dissect a god...

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.400
with alchemy?

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.830
Don't tell me...

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:56.310
the evil-banishing properties of the
 Shenshoujin blocked my alchemy?

00:05:56.950 --> 00:06:00.790
I won't finish you. Just leave you to die.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.810
Your reward for battling a god.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:08.930
You'll have the best seat in the house for 
watching the planet's life be changed.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:14.930
Come back already, Symphogears!

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:19.360
It's time. Rise.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.090
No matter what happens, I won't run anymore.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:42.370
I promise.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.600
What is it? What's going on?

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.040
All these signals...

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:53.920
The Curse of Balal remains
 in effect. So why?

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:58.950
We're getting hacking reports from
 all over the world at the same time.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.890
Multiple reports of damage 
to computer facilities.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.130
Don't tell me... Since she 
can't use human brains,

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:09.060
Shem-ha is using the world's 
computer terminal network.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:15.830
Part of the port side was damaged
 by an external attack!

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.610
We're taking on water!

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:19.570
Yggdrasil is everywhere!

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.150
Not just the one in Kamakura!

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.580
Yggdrasil is all over the world!

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:28.980
Our attempt was a failure.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:32.410
At this rate, we'll have bigger problems 
than saving the Wielders on the moon...

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.110
Thrilling!

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:43.350
Now, with Yggdrasil, I will change all things.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.070
Chris-chan, look!

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.040
Our home...

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.700
What's going on?

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.150
It seems it's begun.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:23.890
Is that... Is that the world you wanted,

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:26.600
where you could be friends with everyone?

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.930
Now that we're perfect monsters 
who can never be human again,

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:38.330
our only way to escape this loneliness 
is turn everyone else into monsters, too.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.660
Is that what you meant by understanding?

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:44.110
Yes!

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:47.150
That's why Shem-ha is remaking 
the world and its life.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:52.680
And we're going to break the Curse of Balal
 to restore her sealed power.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.870
Vanessa... are we going to fight?

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.370
We are.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:01.850
So get back. Big sister's decision.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:11.770
Then, I'll... We'll...

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.750
Warmth, strictness, connections...

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.780
To defend the place that gave us all those...

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:26.950
<i>Killiter Ichaival tron.</i>

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.080
Bang!

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.880
<i>The smell of gunpowder and 
smoke tickles the nose</i>

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:21.000
<i>The clatter of empty gun cartridges</i>

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:26.800
<i>Anybody who's in love with 
the sight of my red heels</i>

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:32.120
<i>and wants a bullet in the 
brain, raise your hand</i>

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:36.320
<i>Even if I'm hurt</i>

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.780
To reclaim the future that was stolen from us,

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:44.000
<i>The winds of time and the bonds 
I have with my companions</i>

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.880
we're going forward!

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:43.600
We don't need to go back to 
how we were, or to change!

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:49.010
<i>Will erase the pain and turn it into a scab</i>

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:49.010
We won't let you go any further.

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:51.580
<i>It's so warm!</i>

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:58.670
<i>Just live your life at 120%</i>

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:09.410
<i>If you do, a better past and future 
will always be in your hands (Fire)</i>

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:11.860
<i>A doubt? A stupid question (Fire)</i>

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.140
<i>No need for introductions—</i>

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.720
I'm just fine!

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:22.120
At this distance...

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:23.860
I'll help you!

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:27.930
You're in the way!

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:29.530
Oh, no!

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:30.620
She's right next to us!

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:34.610
Chris-chan, come with me!

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:36.250
You want me to fight up close?!

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.750
Vanessa!

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:44.380
Take this!

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.600
They're fighting somewhere!

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.070
It must be close!

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:53.310
<i>{naite nanka ine}</i>

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.870
<i>{mada oacha? ine}</i>

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:58.850
<i>It's so warm!</i>

00:11:58.700 --> 00:11:59.820
Vanessa!

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.670
Live! Struggle!

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.640
<i>I've come far enough to pull 
along the hand that holds my own</i>

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:10.650
<i>An honest, foolish futurism</i>

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.480
She's putting the reflector at the front?!

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:16.370
<i>The histories that came 
together will guide us (Fire)</i>

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.090
At least...

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:16.580
we...

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:18.860
<i>Output to full (Fire)</i>

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.880
didn't want...

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:21.330
<i>Locked on (Fire)</i>

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:24.960
<i>Let it go, let loose</i>

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:30.380
<i>Take everything that I've got!</i>

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:27.000
...to be monsters!

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:29.720
<b>AA De Le Metalica</b>

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.490
Why did you save us?

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.530
I didn't save you.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:56.680
But...

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:02.190
If you really want to keep going forward,

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:06.370
you should know that it's even more
 important to have a place to call home.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:12.800
I think too much, so I might 
not be certain about some things.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.850
But because I have a place to call home,

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.310
I can stand up again and keep going.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.050
That goes for you, too.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.400
Vanessa!

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.480
I don't want to do any more of this!

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.700
I don't want the heart of a monster!

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.470
And I'm tired of using my weakness

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:34.000
as an excuse to kill the feelings in my heart...

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:36.850
A place to call home...

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.490
I also...

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.700
But the farce is over.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:44.750
This is the end.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:55.110
I'm taking down that disgusting 
network jammer myself.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.560
Is that you, Shem-ha?

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:02.170
When I recreated her as a perfect monster,

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:04.960
I put a part of myself inside her.

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:09.810
P-Please, God-Killer!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:13.040
Use your fist to strike Shem-ha!

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.880
If I do that, you'll also...

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:23.180
I don't want anybody else to use me!

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.550
Please!

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.910
Please!

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:31.840
God-Killer, I beg of you!

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:40.730
Balwisyall nescell Gungnir tron!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:54.680
A virus program?

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.440
Shem-ha injected it herself?

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:01.820
The fist of a god-killer is a scary thing,

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:05.840
but this is the result of your hesitation.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.300
Vanessa!

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.640
Vanessa-san!

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.750
Don't look so pathetic.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.720
You protected us.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:29.710
Even with your cursed fist, 
you protected our pride.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.630
Tell me! What's happening?

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:38.760
This facility, Murdock, is about 
to create a new Shem-ha.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.590
Like this.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:49.300
Countless thanks, human.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.440
On that day, one year ago,

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:55.730
when mankind was connected for an instant,

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.490
I revived, and rose from Magallanica.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:00.960
A year ago?

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:07.360
Because all of humanity was connected by 
Apple to stop the meteor from falling?

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:10.600
Then what was that song in the noise?

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.900
A fragment of the unified language,

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:15.990
changed in form, having survived
 to the present day.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.810
It was a remnant of that.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:21.390
It wasn't that humanity 
couldn't be connected,

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:24.200
it was that they mustn't be 
allowed to be connected.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:26.700
But knowing the truth won't help.

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:29.680
You'll die here in the ruins.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:35.620
At this rate, we'll die in space 
before we get to go home!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.790
Our Gears! Let's equip our Gears!

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.160
Our Gears won't help us!

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:45.090
Wonderful.

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:47.880
All I hate has turned to dust.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:51.030
The monsters were of great help.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.410
Now I simply wait for the lunar eclipse...

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:58.700
Wh-What is this?

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.760
A philosophical labyrinth 
the three of us created,

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:06.300
over 380,000 kilometers in length!

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:10.060
Not only will it insulate you from
 the explosion's shockwave,

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:15.620
it'll bend space and give 
you a path back to Earth!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:20.210
The fastest, shortest way,
 in a straight line...

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:21.130
But...

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:26.510
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:30.600
There is a curse laid by a 
monster in its last moments...

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:33.200
A last way to resist,

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:37.670
by showing the heroes we hate so much 
that the Earth can no longer be saved...

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:41.020
Yeah. But thank you.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:44.480
Curses can be changed into blessings.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:46.910
That's what my dad said.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.530
And I believe it!

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:54.040
It appears that...

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.690
This is it for us...

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:59.350
We've taken your feelings for our own!

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:03.970
Carrying them on is the 
job of an easygoing girl!

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.830
Yeah. We'll deliver them for you...

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:08.990
To the place we call home!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.910
I hate you all...

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:22.000
Symphogear Wielders, you won't 
let us even be monsters?

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:24.300
Thank you.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:38.390
I didn't know holding hands with 
somebody took so much courage.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:40.710
But I...

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:42.020
Tsubasa-san!

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:49.140
Looking at the Earth like this, 
I don't even know where to return to!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.300
The life that lives on this planet...

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:52.610
Everyone...

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.850
<i>This is HQ! Come in!</i>

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.400
We're a mess, but we're still okay!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.490
And it's not just us!

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:07.430
If Yggdrasil functions using 
the world's computers,

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:10.490
then it can be jammed 
from the network, as well.

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:15.560
Did you use Echelon to set up 
firewalls all over the world?

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:20.400
As President of the United States, 
I am issuing an emergency declaration.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.600
Anyone confident in their skills, 
as well as organizations across the world,

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.630
are hereby requested to fight back 
against this worldwide hacking attempt.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:32.460
We can stop this thing's advance by disrupting 
each terminal's calculation abilities.

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:35.350
Keep it at bay with everything 
humanity can muster!

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:39.020
But the way humanity's working together...

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:43.120
I've been busy delivering a letter

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:48.860
that Yatsuhiro-dono wrote in life, 
requesting aid from all the world's leaders.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.580
<b>Ogawa Clan Leader
Eldest Brother Souji Ogawa</b>

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:53.830
<b>Absolute Zero</b>

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:54.250
This situation wasn't expected...

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.540
<b>Ogawa Clan
Youngest Brother Suteinu Ogawa</b>

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:59.520
I had the IT folks who hang 
out in my bar give me a hand.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.820
Brother! Sute-kun!

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:03.310
Thank you!

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.890
Even when destined to never connect,

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:09.650
the world, and its people,
 still come together.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:14.780
Protectors don't protect the 
world because they're weak,

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:19.270
but because their courage and endless 
strength is worthy of protecting.

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:22.070
Right, Father?

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:27.150
Everyone, Ex-Drive!

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:30.350
But we don't have the phonic 
gain to make it possible!

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:31.410
Just believe...

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:34.100
in the song in our hearts!

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:35.540
In the Symphogears!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.770
<i>Orbit calculated.</i>

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:37.710
<i>But...</i>

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:48.550
<i>Gatrandis babel ziggurat edenal</i>

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:56.290
<i>Emustolronzen fine el baral zizzl</i>

00:20:56.710 --> 00:21:05.480
<i>Gatrandis babel ziggurat edenal</i>

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.370
At that angle of entry...

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:15.840
<i>Emustolronzen fine el zizzl.</i>

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:24.380
They don't have the phonic gain 
needed to activate the Ex-Drive.

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:28.320
You returned from the moon. Astonishing.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.100
But this is your end.

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:35.050
Fall, shooting stars. 
Burn, and burn out.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:40.950
And...
